From 4c9894b990b873172ab1441f0bca33a37f2a2f44 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Phicomm R1 bring-up <r1-bringup@localhost>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 12:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] bluez: export A2DP endpoints before registering app

BlueZ handles Media1.RegisterApplication asynchronously by immediately
querying the application's ObjectManager.  BlueALSA 4.3.1 sends that call
before exporting its endpoint objects, which can leave BlueZ waiting for the
ObjectManager transaction while BlueALSA eventually reports a D-Bus timeout.

Create the ObjectManager, export every configured A2DP endpoint, and only then
send RegisterApplication.  This is the ordering used by current upstream
BlueALSA in bluez_adapter_register_media_application().

Upstream-reference: 894ebe68f69984ebd5d89def72cd0283a870c09b
Signed-off-by: Phicomm R1 bring-up <r1-bringup@localhost>
---
 src/bluez.c | 5 +++--
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/bluez.c b/src/bluez.c
index b0d7cf7..cb9369f 100644
--- a/src/bluez.c
+++ b/src/bluez.c
@@ -145,0 +146,3 @@
+	/* BlueZ must see the endpoints in its first ObjectManager snapshot. */
+	bluez_register_a2dp_all(a);
+
@@ -246 +248,0 @@
-		bluez_register_a2dp_all(a);
--
2.51.0
